    "body": "@snuggs \r\n\r\nI think it would - the introduction of a new element would already do it, I think. At least the [W3 validator](https://validator.w3.org/nu/#textarea) rejects the following input:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n<head><title>Title</title></head>\r\n<body>\r\n<bind var=\"variableName\"/>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe standard would need to be extended, and validators updated - but that would be the case for any syntax using the `<` character.",
